Z||000000||KevinP||07-19-2000||12:20 AM||||If any of you caught that post by SeanyD about the front enigine fiero, take another look.  If it's possible to relocate the engine to the front, then what's left in the back?  My question is: Is it then possible to do some cutting and find a way to throw a pair of buckets in the back?  I'm sure that there are some practicality and structural problems involved, but I never said it would be easy! I've seen people with glass hatches on their fastbacks that cover the rear.  All you would need to do is find a way to hold the seats (as far as frame is concerned), and a way to seal it all up.  Maybe my imagination is getting carried away, but I figured I'd throw it out there and hear what you guys thought!<BR>Latta'<P>Kevin<P>PS--check out <A HREF="http://www.boomtastic.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.boomtastic.com</A> <BR>||||reg||3
